     "note": "GO-WITH-CHANGES (badge A). FOUND THE DEFECT THAT SURVIVED THE FIRST FOLLOW-UP, and it is this project's own vacuity class committed BY the round closing that class: dropping the .get defaults DECAPITATED gate 2's OTHER driver selftest, because a THIRD rig dict (selftest_logdir's) declared neither key - and both its rows kept passing, since the log files open BEFORE the raise. Caught it by TIMING: 1.573 s and 15 driver lines became 0.062 s and one, still PASS. Also: the straddle cannot see a mutant that scales BOTH the print and the comparison - only the literal config-pin row can, so deriving the over-leg from the printed value REMOVED a redundancy; `>` -> `>=` scores zero red rows; and my orphan-child justification was UNMEASURED (it measured zero survivors both ways). Confirmed `used` is populated on every path, and that /tmp/gxregress was untouched.",
