    "note": "REVIEWED AND FOLLOWED UP: 863d238 (round) + b9daca1 (records) + cdc4849 (follow-up). Eight of nine seats answered; none found anything wrong with the three shipped fixes -- the domain clamp, the catch-up bound, the RTC narrowing and the above-the-early-out placement were each confirmed by every seat that could trace them. EVERY DEFECT FOUND WAS IN THE INSTRUMENT OR THE RECORDS. Detector 14 -> 24 rows; gate 2 148 -> 157 checks; census 13 mutants, 13 killed, 0 survived, 0 faults. The generalisable finding: reading a constant from the header defeats transcription drift AND creates blindness to the constant itself, so a row must also assert an absolute consequence. Regression review batched to Sunday night per P12.  [A: the diff under review was mine, disclosed.]"
