     "note": "REFRAMED THE ROUND: the panel's 300:1 spread on the ceiling is itself evidence that A FIXED CEILING IS THE WRONG INSTRUMENT - the measured harm is iterations per signal, and even the largest proposed ceiling leaves ~153,846 of them. The catch-up CAP is the protection; the ceiling is domain normalisation. Also: the report belongs at the CLAMP SITE (device context, where fatal() is already idiom), not in the handler - and the SIGALRM hazard codex worried about does not exist there. NaN is caught by NEGATING the comparisons that must exist anyway, at zero marginal cost: A FREE GUARD AT A TRUST BOUNDARY NEEDS NO REACHABILITY PROOF. Committed against shipping the loop bound alone, because interval=0 would then burn the cap every signal for ever.",
