   "witness": "none -- host-side only. Reachable from the `-d` argument and the config file, never by a guest, so no rung-3/4 witness can exist. Pinning the exact truncated value needs a build.",
   "state_note": "*** EVIDENCE 2026-08-27: TRUE, host-side only -- AND IT IS HALF OF A FAMILY, which neither seat could see from its own row. ***\n\n`src/disk/diskimage.c:1722` reads `override_base_offset = atoi(fname);`. **`atoi` returns `int`**, while the field is 64-bit -- `:1729-1730` prints it with `PRIi64`. A 64-bit-capable option is parsed by a 32-bit function.\n\nThe `< 0` check at `:1728` catches a result that lands negative, but **not a truncation that wraps to a plausible positive value**, which is the silent case.\n\n*** THE FAMILY: THIS IS A MISSED SITE FROM `#414`. *** `:1681` says *\"#414: strtoll, not atoi, and BOTH fields\"* -- that round converted the GEOMETRY fields at `:1693`/`:1698` and left the base offset on `atoi`. See [[b122]], the same round's OTHER residual (converted, but the endptr discarded). **Two rows, one incomplete conversion.**\n\n**NOT guest-reachable**: `diskimage_add()` has exactly two callers, `main.c:707` (`-d`) and `emul_parse.c:558` (config), both at startup. Severity is host-input robustness.\n\n"
  },
