     "note": "TRUE, AND THE FILED WORDING UNDERSTATES IT -- the only item on this brief the seat MEASURED rather than read. diskimage_scsicmd.c:915-931 fsyncs only d->f and its own TODO at :922-924 says overlays and bitmaps should be too; with an overlay, fwrite_helper writes ONLY to the overlay (diskimage.c:1291-1302), so SYNCHRONIZE CACHE syncs the one file with no new data in it. THE BIGGER HALF: it does not even sync d->f, because :926 calls fsync(fileno(d->f)) with NO fflush -- while diskimage.c:1208-1210 carries the comment explaining exactly why fflush must come first. do_fsync defaults to 0, so nothing is flushed at write time either. HOST PROBE, _exit() to simulate host death: 512B written -> 0 persisted (512 LOST); 4096 -> 0 (4096 LOST); 8192 -> 4096 (4096 LOST); fflush+fsync in the diskimage.c shape -> PERSISTED.  [panel_20260817_174701]"
