     "note": "FLAGSHIP REVIEW of the shipped rounds. Badge `s`. It re-derived every claim from the repo rather than accepting the ledger, and ran no gates or builds.\n* *** IT FOUND gate_hygiene LATENTLY RED AT HEAD -- MEASURED by recomputing that gate's own probe_code() census read-only. *** cf4b083 added luna_intmask_probe.py carrying all three pinned #392 constructs and did NOT move EXPECT_CONVERTED from 16. Confirmed by running gate 6: log-hygiene FAIL, 3 of 48. The commit ran gate 2 and the float selftest; GATE 6 NEVER FIRED. It would have failed the Aug 22 weekly battery as a hygiene regression with a bookkeeping cause -- the phantom-regression class.\n* AND THE ROOT CAUSE WAS THAT THE PROBE SHIPPED UNWIRED, so nothing forced a gate run. Its structural point, now in the gate's annotation: a probe that ships WITH its wiring cannot skip the pin. Wiring it into gate 11 immediately proved that twice -- the run found the hygiene red AND that build/'s BINARY was four hours stale (source 18:08 with the fix, binary 13:58 without it), so any measurement against that tree since would have been of the wrong code. The probe reported PRE_FIX_SYMPTOM rather than a confusing failure, which is a detector giving a legible answer when its input is wrong.\n* THE THIRD TIME THIS GATE WENT RED FOR THIS REASON, and the second was ONE COMMIT EARLIER THE SAME DAY: the footbridge probe had the identical coupling, a subagent warned about it, it was handled correctly, the annotation recording the lesson was written -- and then the same mistake was made with a different probe. Reading a lesson is not having it.\n* #437 VERDICT: SHIP STANDS, and it called the detector 'the most self-honest artifact I have reviewed in this tree' -- having re-derived the four mutants' trace strings against the shipped loop rather than trusting the header's table. Both residuals CORRECTLY FILED: m437multi is a conservative over-report that FAILS SAFE (guest told unsafe when safe), and m437rtmp's worst framing was already dodged in the shipped comment, which uses R: only to justify not touching the read-only base handle. ONE COUPLING TO CARRY: the 1b row pins status==0x02 for exactly the m437multi scenario and the gate greps that row by name, so an m437multi fix must move detector and gate greps in the SAME commit."
    },
