     "ev": "codex 5.6-SOL xhigh, fired against the row's own hold_question (_scratchpad/holdq_briefs/holdq_ovsync.md; answer at scratchpad/holdq_out/ovsync.txt) -- RESEARCH phase",
     "note": "*** GO-WITH-CHANGES (RESEARCH phase, answered separately by the same codex seat -- its answer gave all three of this row's held stages their own disposition, and only ASSESS was recorded on the first pass). *** The `diskimage_sync()` design is RIGHT; what is incomplete is COMMAND-FAMILY coverage. `4d0981d` handles SYNCHRONIZE CACHE(10) / 0x35 correctly on every constructed state: writable flat images get `fflush` then `fsync`; every attached overlay's data gets that pair before its bitmap; any failure sets the result false and the handler returns CHECK CONDITION rather than GOOD. **But SYNCHRONIZE CACHE(16) / 0x91 is not defined or handled at all.** Verified independently: `diskimage_scsicmd.c` contains only `SCSICMD_SYNCHRONIZE_CACHE` (0x35); a valid 16-byte 0x91 CDB passes the group-length check, falls to the unimplemented default, and `dev_asc.c:1284-1287` converts ABSENT status to `0x00` GOOD. The remedy is a choice, not a design: route 0x91 through the same helper, or reject it with CHECK CONDITION / ILLEGAL REQUEST."
