     "note": "*** VERDICT: THE DEFECT IS REAL, BUT THE CITED WITNESS DOES NOT WITNESS IT -- AND THE ROW IS INTERNALLY CONFLATED. DOCUMENTED-ONLY/CLOSE under the stopping rule. *** EVERY ELEMENT RE-VERIFIED HERE BEFORE IT WAS ACTED ON, because this answer was used to correct the carrier: the row's `witness` field is None; its closure names 'the MIPS compare write ... converts the distance to a deadline into a frequency'; the row mentions ARM Footbridge four times and MIPS CP0 zero times; and `footbridge_sites_probe.py:111` execs `-E cats`, an ARM/SA110 machine that executes no MIPS instruction and cannot reach CP0 Compare. That probe returned entirely CORRECT values (vendor 0x1011; 0x00345678 after storing 0x12345678 -- the missing byte is the Footbridge's deliberate 24-bit mask signature, not an error). Its cited `dev_footbridge.c:548` is stale: :548 is `console_putchar` and the timer mask is at :640. **So a witness WAS built, and it witnesses a different path from the one this row's closure defines.** THE MIPS MECHANISM IS SOURCE-DEMONSTRABLE AND WORSE THAN 'a different internal representation': a Compare write installs a PERIODIC host timer (`cpu_mips_coproc.c:796`), every expiry increments `compare_interrupts_pending` (:418), and a guest Compare write acknowledges only ONE pending event while clearing Cause.IP7 (:822). If two or more callbacks have accumulated, the next dyntrans update re-asserts IP7 before any new Count==Compare event -- **a wrong guest-readable Cause value and an extra interrupt exception**, not an observationally equivalent model. IT ALSO KEPT THE EVIDENCE LADDER HONEST: the ~615,384-callbacks-per-signal figure came from a timer-core SCRATCH probe, not an end-to-end MIPS guest observation; and the 40.2-second guest clock freeze that was measured belongs to the separate `fbpending` overflow defect, whose #442 bound is in today's source. Neither witnesses MIPS `dfreq`. *** CONSEQUENCE ACTED ON: CLAUDE.md's line 'dfreq's [no-witness claim] was measured false by building the witness in one session' is a WRONG RECORD and was corrected in both carrier copies. The RULE -- that 'no witness of either kind' is checkable and must be checked -- is untouched and remains one of the most useful lines in the file. ***"
