e raw `Rn` and the code writes its running raw `addr` back.  The generated optimised path\nconfirms the intended shape independently: select the page from the raw address, mask the\naccess offset with `addr &= 0xffc`, update the base register from the UNMASKED value.\n\n**A QUALIFICATION THE RECORD MUST CARRY, and the seat volunteered it rather than ratifying:**\n`ARM_CONTROL_ALIGN` is initialised ENABLED but is never enforced by any memory access.  So\nthe record may NOT say unqualifiedly that the fast path is *the architectural answer* -- it is\nthe answer for the emulator's implemented A=0/U=0 behaviour, and **at the advertised A=1 state\nBOTH paths are wrong**, because an alignment exception is owed and neither raises one.\n\n**(b) RANKING -- ANSWERED: above `b120r`.**  And the question's own framing was wrong too:\n`fable_queue.md` ALREADY ranks this first among the five triage rows, so it was never sitting\nbehind boot-witnessed items.  The seat declined to generalise, correctly: this does NOT put it\nabove every boot-witnessed durability-loss or host-death defect, which need individual harm\ncomparisons.\n\n*** THE ONE THING STILL GENUINELY OWED, and it is a DURABLE-ARTIFACT gap rather than a\nreasoning gap: the rung-3 probe is PRIVATE AND UNCOMMITTED. ***  The seat could not certify\nit in a read-only session because no artifact exists under `regress/`.  So its endorsement of\nthe WITNESS is READ-from-record while the manual-and-source finding stands on its own -- and\nthe row's `witness` field being empty is CONSISTENT with that, not an oversight.  **A\nreproduction whose artifact lives nowhere durable cannot be re-verified by anyone**, which is\nthe volatile-path rule aimed at a probe instead of a log.\n\n*Recorded because the answer existed for three days in an entry nobody had acted on.  This is\nthe unread-review class -- the most expensive shape this project has -- caught by reading the\nrow's own entries before starting new work on it.*"
