     "note": "IMPLEMENTED AS #520 by the main loop (running as Opus 5 after the owner switched the session model; the design ruling this implements was made by the loop as Fable 5.1 on 2026-09-09 and is unchanged).  THE RULING'S OWN PRECONDITION WAS CHECKED FIRST AND IS DISCHARGED: it required the witness to have been re-baselined on a tree carrying #514 (3031a30, committed 08:38:00), and the witness artifacts are dated 08:56-08:57 the same morning -- eighteen minutes later, so no re-run was owed.  THE FIX: `a0' is a uint64_t, so `if (a0 >= 1)' was an UNSIGNED compare and BOTH negative selectors the arm's own header documents as invalidate-EVERYTHING (-1 and -2) compared GREATER than 1 and took the single-VADDR branch; a guest TBIA/TBIAP flushed one page and left every other cached translation live.  Now `if ((int64_t)a0 >= 1 && (int64_t)a0 <= 3)' -- a two-sided SIGNED range, so 0 and 4.. join the negatives on the conservative arm.  ONE executable line; the rest of the diff is comment.  NO ANNOUNCE, per the ruling (every selector now takes a conservative-correct arm, so there is no event to report and the addition licence forbids a diagnostic with no measured delta).  MEASURED INDEPENDENTLY BY THE LOOP in a fresh scratch clone of build/ (/tmp/gx520, baseline NAMED as HEAD's blob and cmp'd, rebuilt per leg, `[ binary -nt source ]' checked, sentinel dropped and cleared, NO project tree written): HEAD 5/7 with `tbia obs' and `tbiap obs' RED (HEAD_run1.out), the fix 7/7 (FIX520_run1.out), both logs ending ALPHATBI_DONE, and ZERO compiler warnings on the edited file in either leg.  That replicates agy's 2026-09-08 witness on a second build at the current HEAD, so test-first is satisfied twice over.  *** THE ROUND IS NOT SHIPPABLE YET: the de-escalation clause owes THREE ACCEPT ROWS and the existing positive control (a0=2) CANNOT carry them *** -- its oracle is `the observing load returns the remapped value', which BOTH arms produce, so it detects an omitted invalidation and not an over-invalidation.  The replacement design is codex's (codex_rows_20260910.txt), verified by it against the cache implementation: two pages per row, a TARGET that is invalidated and an UNRELATED page that must SURVIVE a selective invalidate, with BOTH remapped so the observation can tell the arms apart.  Handed to the Opus measuring seat to build and kill-table.  TWO L4s IN MY OWN NEW COMMENT, caught by codex before commit and corrected: I had reversed which entries the selector spares (-1 invalidates the ASM=0 entries and SPARES the ASM=1 ones), and the arm's upstream header still said `a0 is ignored for now. TODO.' which #520 makes false."
