   "opened": "2026-09-07",
   "title": "PAL_clrfen (0xae) is named and user-mode-whitelisted but has NO case, so a guest call reaches the default arm and stops the CPU",
   "witness": "none",
   "entries": [],
   "commits": "",
   "state_note": "Volunteered by the grok seat under the found-something-else licence while enumerating every\n`apcb_flags` reader for [[alphaswpctxptbr]]'s fix review, 2026-09-07.\n\n`PAL_clrfen` is *named* in the palcode file and appears in the user-mode whitelist, but the\ndispatch switch has **no `case` for it** -- so a guest that calls it falls to the default arm,\nwhich sets `cpu->running = 0` and stops the machine.\n\n**NOT verified by me** -- recorded as the seat reported it, and a round on this owes the reading\nfirst.  It is the same shape as [[alphaswpctxptbr]] (a PAL entry that does not do what its name\nsays) and plausibly the same family as the option-set work: an unimplemented PAL call is member 7\nterritory (IMPLEMENT) rather than a decline, because declining a context-flag operation leaves the\nmachine in a state the guest cannot reason about."
  },
