   "id": "gateworktree",
   "sev": "med",
   "state": "open",
   "opened": "2026-09-07",
   "title": "precommit_check.sh validates the WORKING TREE, not the staged content, so it cannot see a staging omission",
   "witness": "none",
   "entries": [
    {
     "seat": "codex",
     "phase": "assess",
     "d": "y",
     "date": "2026-09-08",
     "grade": "ANSWERED",
     "outcome": "CONFIRMED and WIDENED: the gate mixes staged FILENAMES with WORKING-TREE CONTENTS; section D is worse -- fully staging empties its input",
     "grader": "main-loop",
     "ev": "regress/artifacts/gateworktree/codex_assess_20260908.txt",
     "note": "ASSESS (FILE-READING).  14,102 b.  Audited all 21 sections against their actual inputs, corrected two claims in my brief, and produced a SHIPPED instance plus a measured instance on this session own commit."
    }
   ],
   "commits": "",
   "state_note": "MEASURED on my own commit, 2026-09-07.  `2956c7e` committed regress/sgi_mte_fill_probe.py and NOT the check_probe_wiring.py MANIFEST entry that classifies it, so a fresh clone at that SHA reds with `UNCLASSIFIED'.  **precommit_check.sh reported PRECOMMIT_PASS 0 hard immediately before that commit**, because the working tree already carried the manifest edit -- it was simply never staged.\n\n    git show HEAD:tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py | grep -c sgi_mte_fill_probe.py  -> 0\n    grep -c sgi_mte_fill_probe.py tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py                  -> 1\n\n> **A CHECK THAT VALIDATES A STATE OTHER THAN THE ONE THAT SHIPS CANNOT SEE A STAGING OMISSION.**  This is NOT the check-that-cannot-fail shape -- the gate failed eleven times tonight and every failure was real.  Its SUBJECT is one step to the left of the thing it guards.\n\n*** IT INTERACTS WITH A POLICY THIS PROJECT ALREADY HOLDS, which is why it is a row and not a note. ***  The carrier forbids `git add -A' and directory adds, so every commit here stages by EXPLICIT PATH.  That is strictly safer against INCLUDING the wrong file -- the failure the rule was written for -- and strictly MORE EXPOSED to OMITTING the right one.  **Two rules pulling opposite ways, and only one of them has a checker.**\n\nThe same commit also missed its own pass-2 receipt (caught by section F) and the ledger row naming it (section L), both on the NEXT commit.  So the gate's coverage is real; what it cannot do is bind that coverage to the staged set.\n\n**THE OBVIOUS FIX IS REJECTED ON ITS OWN RISK:** running the gate under `git stash --keep-index' would let a mid-run crash lose uncommitted work, and the gate takes ~2 minutes.  That is worse than the defect.  **The narrower candidate** is an existence check over the STAGED set for known file PAIRS -- a new `regress/*.py' and its MANIFEST entry; a `src/' change and a CHANGELOG round block -- in the check_cited_artifacts.py idiom (existence-only, forward-only from a cutoff).  NOT BUILT: it changes what every commit must satisfy, which is an owner decision, and owes two negative controls -- red on a probe staged without its manifest entry, green when both are staged.\n\n*** CONFIRMED BY codex AND WIDER THAN I FILED IT.  THE GATE SELECTS FILES FROM THE INDEX AND\nTHEN READS THEIR CONTENTS FROM THE WORKING TREE. ***\n\n    CHANGED=$(git diff --cached --name-only)      <- NAMES, from the index\n    cmp -s \"$SEC/$f\" \"$EST/$f\"                    <- BYTES, from the filesystem\n\n**There is NO indexed-blob reader -- no `git show :<path>` -- anywhere in the invoked checking\npaths.**  `git ls-files` appears, but that tests index MEMBERSHIP, not content; L's `git show`\nretrieves filenames from an existing COMMIT.  codex audited all 21 sections and marks 18 of them\nfalse-green/false-reject on content: a working-tree correction can conceal an invalid indexed\nversion, and working-tree damage can reject a valid one.\n\n*** SECTION D IS THE WORST AND IT IS THE OPPOSITE SHAPE: IT READS **UNSTAGED** ADDITIONS, SO THE\nMORE CORRECTLY YOU STAGE, THE LESS IT CHECKS. ***\n\n    ADDED=$(git diff -U0 | grep '^+' | grep -v '^+++')\n\n**MEASURED ON THIS SESSION'S OWN COMMIT, and it is exact.**  At `#513`'s gate run the only\ntracked-modified-but-unstaged file was `regress/sgi_de_primop_probe.py`, which is deliberately\nkept OUT of every commit -- `git show --stat e302c98 | grep -c sgi_de_primop_probe` is **0**.  So\nD's two green rows, *\"no new file:line citations\"* and *\"no added occurrence counts\"*, were\ncomputed **entirely from a file that is not in the commit**, while 129 staged files were invisible\nto it.  A fully-staged commit gives D the empty set and D reports green on it.\n\n> **That is the check-that-cannot-fail family in its purest form: not a badly written assertion,\n> but a check whose input goes to zero exactly when the thing it guards is done properly.**\n\n*** A SHIPPED INSTANCE, found by codex in history rather than argued: commit `2956c7e` added\n`regress/sgi_mte_fill_probe.py` while its own `check_probe_wiring.py` carried ZERO manifest\nentries for that file. ***  An actual shipped invariant violation of this class.  (codex was\nexplicit that it did not verify historical gate OUTPUT -- the violation is established from the\ncommit contents, not from a green row.)\n\n*** TWO CORRECTIONS TO MY BRIEF, BOTH LOAD-BEARING FOR SECTION J. ***\n* I described J as comparing two tracked files.  **The project-root originals are OUTSIDE the git\n  repository**; only the `GXEMUL-SEC/tools/` copies are in the index.  So J's\n  `cmp -s \"$ROOT/$_c\" \"$SEC/tools/$_c\"` compares an UNTRACKED external file against a tracked\n  copy -- and updating the external original and its working copy while omitting the copy from\n  staging lets J pass while the commit retains the OLD carrier.\n* **J's tracked-copy existence test is a bare `-f`.**  It does not verify index membership at all.\n\n*** THE FIX IS NOT A FLAG, AND codex NAMED THE TRAP IN THE OBVIOUS ONE. ***  Blindly replacing\nreads with `git show \":$path\"` would inspect the WRONG version during the common before-staging\nrun, because *\"nothing staged\" normally means the index equals HEAD, not that the index is\nempty*.  The shape it prescribes:\n\n* **announce a SNAPSHOT MODE before the first pipeline invocation**, not at the late `CHANGED`\n  assignment -- INDEX mode (membership, contents and checker selftests all from the candidate\n  index; D switches to `git diff --cached -U0`) or WORKING-TREE PREVIEW (keep the useful\n  before-staging audit; D keeps `git diff -U0`);\n* keep the deliberately EXTERNAL inputs -- carrier originals, build trees, panel dirs -- and the\n  historical git queries explicitly separate, since those are correct as filesystem reads;\n* the helpers derive their paths from `__file__`, **so redirecting the shell's `ROOT` is not\n  sufficient** -- a complete isolated index snapshot (a worktree) is the practical route, and it\n  must carry unchanged dependencies too;\n* byte comparisons need a deliberate decision about git filters and newline conversion (locally\n  the carrier copies are LF and `core.autocrlf` is false).\n\n**SEVERITY: this does not change what any product code does.  What it changes is what a GREEN GATE\nMEANS**, on every round this project has recorded -- which is why it is filed high among harness\nitems rather than as a tidy-up.  It is a tooling change owing negative controls in both directions\n(prove a staged-only defect REDS in index mode; prove a working-tree-only defect does NOT), so it\nships as its own harness round, never as a rider."
  },
