     "note": "READ THE TREE (both handlers, the decoder, cpu_m88k_instr.c, generate_arm_r.c, cpu.h, regress/*.py, DDI 0100I).  *** REACHED THE BFI FINDING INDEPENDENTLY OF CODEX AND FROM A DIFFERENT ROUTE: \"BFI also builds (1 << width) - 1 after width = msb - lsb + 1, so the 'BFI is correct' contrast may be wrong\" -- and BFI was the CONTRAST CASE in my brief, inlined as the one that is right, because I had checked only its decoder. ***  Settled two facts nothing else could: DDI 0100I contains NO UBFX/SBFX/BFI (so the encoding-legality premise has no local primary source and no page may be cited), and regress/ contains no ubfx/sbfx rows.  Said RUNG-3 IS ACHIEVABLE -- confirmed by construction afterwards.  Flagged HONESTLY that it set out to measure the host lowering and did NOT finish, so \"the mask becomes 0\" stayed a prediction until the witness measured it.",
