     "note": "*** THE ANSWER THIS ROUND TURNS ON. ***  Ratified the mask/guard/1U form at 1, 31, 32 and the && reorder, then found THREE one-line escapes that score full marks -- and, more valuably, showed that TWO OF THEM CANNOT BE CLOSED BY ANY ROW: `1U`->`1` and restoring topBitMask are DEFINEDNESS repairs, and definedness has no guest-visible value on a non-trapping host (1 << 31 and 1U << 31 give the same mask after the - 1; with a correct 32-bit mask x |= ~mask is x |= 0).  **It also showed `s w32` pins the MASK, not topBitMask -- the probe comment calling it \"the second-UB row\" was wrong.**  The THIRD escape -- deleting the bit test so width < 32 always sign-extends -- IS observable and is closed in-round by `s clear`.  Refused five comment overclaims, caught the 496-count, and caught that MY OWN comment-heavy patch shifted the decoder citations I had put in the brief.",
