     "note": "PASS-2 FOLLOW-UP, and its headline is a FALSE CLAIM IN A COMMIT MESSAGE THAT CANNOT BE EDITED.\n\ncodex's pass-2 BODY was read AFTER `c0c7f55' had launched.  Its finding: the round asserted -- in the probe comment, in the CHANGELOG block AND in the commit message -- that the pc control holds \"on EVERY row, w32 included\".  **IT DID NOT.**  Only `pc adv', `mid pc' and `w32 pc' asserted pc, and all three are MOV/UBFX rows.  **NO SBFX ROW CHECKED PC AT ALL** -- and the SBFX rows are exactly the ones whose expected failure value is ALSO exactly zero, i.e. the case the pc control exists to disambiguate.  Verified by listing the rows rather than by re-reading the claim.\n\nA SECOND, QUIETER GAP WENT WITH IT: `s w31' did not exist, so the round's headline claim -- \"only the width-32 case is observable\" -- rested on a UBFX width-31 row and was generalised to SBFX with no evidence.  That is the copy-the-neighbour defect the sbfx comment block had ALREADY been corrected for once in the same round.\n\nFOLLOW-UP SHIPPED: `s w32 pc' and `s w31' added (11 -> 14 rows), measured **14/14** on the fixed build with all three build trees CLEAN/FRESH and est/ CLEAN (part 2 N/A, source tree).  The source half is COMMENT-ONLY and was PROVEN so rather than asserted: comment delimiters 317/317 before and after, the three #510 code expressions identical in count, and stripping all comments from both revisions gives BYTE-IDENTICAL files.\n\n*** A CITATION OF MINE DECAYED INSIDE ONE EVENING -- AND GIT GAVE IT BACK. *** The follow-up re-ran the probe with a `>' redirect onto `witness_FIXED12_20260907.raw', so the working-tree copy held a 14-row run while the CHANGELOG cited it for 12/12.  Caught because the claim was CONTRADICTED BY ITS OWN EVIDENCE rather than merely unverifiable.  **The artifact was COMMITTED, so `git checkout' restored it byte-for-byte; the 12/12 is genuine and IS cited.**  All four scores now stand on their own logs: 9/11, 11/11, 12/12, 14/14.\n\n*** AND MY FIRST CORRECTION OF THIS WAS ITSELF WRONG, which is the more useful record. *** I wrote into both the CHANGELOG and this row that the measurement was GONE and NOT CITABLE, and only then checked git.  A correction carries MORE authority than the error it corrects, so it earns a second reading, not less of one -- this project already budgets a second review pass for records-correction rounds and this is why.  The rule vindicated is also not the one I reached for: the durable path held because it was UNDER VERSION CONTROL.  An identical clobber of an uncommitted artifact -- anything in `_scratchpad/', or a run whose commit has not happened yet -- is unrecoverable.\n\nTHREE STRING-ANCHORED EDIT ATTEMPTS REFUSED BEFORE ONE SUCCEEDED (matched 2, matched 2, matched 0), because the #510 comment block is DUPLICATED in X(ubfx) and X(sbfx) and because I retyped its wording from memory.  The guard did its job every time and wrote nothing.  The working form LOCATES by searching the real file and REPLACES BY LINE RANGE, bottom-up -- no whitespace guessed, no anchor able to hit the wrong copy."
