   "title": "three unreachable size guards and one always-true test in dev_dec21143.c -- bufsize is bounded to 0..2047 by its own masks",
   "witness": "none",
   "entries": [
    {
     "seat": "codex",
     "phase": "assess",
     "d": "✓",
     "date": "2026-09-07",
     "grade": "ANSWERED",
     "outcome": "three-dead-one-always-true",
     "grader": "main-loop",
     "ev": "regress/artifacts/queueunrated/codex_bitsbytes_20260907.txt",
     "note": "THE EVIDENCE FOR THIS ROW, cited here for the first time -- the row existed and the answer that established it was uncited.  Derivation: `buf1_size = tdes1 & TDCTL_SIZE1' and `buf2_size = (tdes1 & TDCTL_SIZE2) >> TDCTL_SIZE2_SHIFT' with masks 0x000007ff and 0x003ff800 shift 11 (tulipreg.h), so BOTH range 0..2047 and so does their selection.  Therefore `bufsize < 0' (twice) and `bufsize > 65536' are ALWAYS FALSE and their clamps are inert.  *** IT DREW THE BOUNDARY ITSELF: the neighbouring `bufsize > 65536 - d->cur_tx_buf_len' is NOT established dead, because it involves the accumulated length. *** Separately `writeback_len > 1' is always true (initialised 4, never reassigned) and is redundant rather than a format-selection error -- it declined to call that a defect."
    }
