     "outcome": "VERDICT: RATIFY THE FIX, DO NOT SHIP THE DETECTOR.  *** THE ROUND'S HIGHEST-VALUE FINDING: M4_condwrite in the MIRROR POLARITY (`&& writeflag == MEM_WRITE') SWEEPS THE ELEVEN-ROW PROBE CLEAN, and my own PRETABLE CHANNEL line claimed `t1 alias' killed it. ***  Root cause is the ADDRESS not the polarity: every alias row used dev 0, an EMPTY slot, where forwarding returns the same all-ones the refusal synthesises -- blind by construction.  Verified all six premises against the fork tree and CORRECTED P4: the 0x00000003 high dword is not from PCIINIT(i82378zb) (which never writes offset 4) but from bus_pci_add's default IO|MEM enable.",
