     "outcome": "NOT RATIFY.  The disposition is right; the instrument does not defend it.  Predicted from the source that `irq latched` is VACUOUS because isa_interrupt_common is edge-triggered and the UART never drops IRR -- CONFIRMED by mutant M1_unlatch scoring a clean sweep with the count still 1.  Also corrected a shipping comment: cpu_dyntrans.c delivers for FIVE architectures, not three; my enumeration keyed on irq_asserted, a correlate.  Confirmed P4 and the empty-set de-escalation reasoning, and stated plainly that it had not re-run the probes.",
