     "note": "[A] ADJUDICATED BY THE MAIN LOOP RUNNING AS FABLE 5.1.  *** THE REPAIR CHAIN CLOSES ON PASS 3. ***  Pass 3 (six seats, none ratifying) found ZERO floor breaches -- every finding was denominator accounting, an L4 in the contract text, a width disclosure, or a coverage observation.  The accounting defect was real and is now MEASURED rather than argued: table H (TABLE_H.out, instrument byte-identical to G's frozen copy) built the two assignment-bit-swap cells four seats found unswept -- M14 8/12 (assert once 4, deassert once 0), M15 11/12 (deassert once 2) -- so the denominator is 2 sites x 8 edits = 16 cells, 14 killed, 2 measured equivalent (M8: the aggregate is 0 until the first assert, and old_isa_assert is recomputed at every entry, never stored; M_nonull: dev_lca.c:498-500 is the only registration, extra never NULL), plus the null medium and two composites whose inclusion had inflated the earlier count.  The contract L4 (grok) is corrected in place; the row() calls are verified byte-identical to the measured instrument, so the correction is records, not floor-bound material, and no pass 4 is owed.  DISCLOSED under clause (e), with warrants: no base-run pin on the second line's assert EDGE (lcairqedgepin); the [G] readback's 8-byte width (measured 0x8, clamped).  THREE DEFECTIVE REPAIRS PRECEDED THE CLEAN ONE in this round -- the loop's disjunction patch (never applied), the seat's verbosity-dependent row, the loop's un-stepped readback (base 11/12) -- which is the measured case for the rule that a repair owes its own pass.  Self-review disclosed: the loop ran the round; the independent evidence is the four panels' seat entries above and the Opus seat's measured tables.",
