     "grader": "main-loop (Fable 5.1)",
     "note": "MEASURING seat (Agent tool), pass 2 on the repair.  M12 IS REACHABLE AND IS A FLOOR BREACH (L2): the ns16550 on IRQ 4 asserts SYNCHRONOUSLY from DEVICE_ACCESS(ns16550) (dev_ns16550_tick inline at four sites, behind com_mcr & MCR_IENABLE), installed unconditionally by bus_isa_init -- edge trace `LCAEDGE 1 assert warned=0x0' -> IER/MCR stores -> `LCAEDGE 2 assert warned=0x1', no deassert between.  Corrected the loop's derivation: isa_interrupt_common asserts on ANY change to a different NONZERO aggregate, so dropping one of two pending lines is also an assert edge.  Supplied and MEASURED the 12-row repair (base 12/12, M12 11/12 with assert once = 3, every existing kill preserved) and flagged its own `uart live' row as verbosity-dependent (replaced by the loop with a com_mcr readback).  Q4: M8's CONCLUSION survives but the loop's stated REASON was false -- 'nothing sets IRR but an assert' is wrong (masked asserts set IRR without entering the stub); the correct warrant is over the AGGREGATE.  Q3: the `kbc attrib' operand widening costs ZERO kills (its red set is a strict subset of `kbc kill's) but the new LABEL `died-outside-lca' is MEASURABLY FALSE (M14: a silent death INSIDE the deassert stub) -- now `no-lca-diagnostic'.  Sharpened: three of the eleven rows cannot kill alone (want-string prefixes).  One unmeasured cell named (drop `d != NULL') -- measured equivalent in table G.  31 raws preserved, all with sentinels."
