   "title": "Alpha has NO interrupt delivery -- #516's decline is the disposition, this is the SUBSYSTEM it declines into.  cd.alpha.irq_asserted is written (cpu_alpha.c:218,:223) and read nowhere; cpu_dyntrans.c delivers for FIVE architectures and has no Alpha arm; memory_rw.c's failed-device branch dispatches only for MIPS and M88K.  Implementing it is dyntrans dispatch + PALcode entry + the IPL check -- its own round.  NOT a host-kill and lower than the kills it grew from: Alpha interrupts have never worked on this tree, #516 only stopped the host dying.  No guest that NEEDS delivery has been measured; the row claims the mechanism is absent, not that a guest is blocked.",
   "note": "Filed 2026-09-09 from the #516 adjudication (option-set member 7, IMPLEMENT), so the missing feature is TRACKED rather than buried inside a fixed kill -- the anti-laundering move the adjudication named."
  },
