   "title": "The THREE altoffset WDC differentials as ONE instrument -- wdc_altoffset_probe.py and the two that `import wdc_altoffset_probe as W' (_sig, _4bit): one module, one rig (-E evbmips -e malta, the battery's own _images/wdc-scratch-64m.img), one media family (the `c' in ciR: is a PREFIX -- MEASURED, the same image attaches as an IDE CD-ROM).  OWED: (a) the parent's `ok' -- already a complete verdict over 18 explicit expectations -- gets an exit status, FIRST QUESTION being whether a nonzero exit breaks the two-leg driver; (b) _4bit's single-leg form is an ORACLE CHOICE (its verdict is definitionally between-leg -- 'its whole point is that it DIFFERS by leg', :216), so the round chooses the fix-side absolute and says so; (c) _sig's `sig' oracle is NON-DISCRIMINATING (unreadable and unrelated values both read as 'declined') and is REDESIGNED, not bolted onto.  Each of the three wiringcliff exemptions is re-dated naming THIS row and DELETED in the same edit as its wiring.",
