   "id": "lcaiocstat0",
   "sev": "med",
   "opened": "2026-09-10",
   "state": "open",
   "witness": "none",
   "commits": null,
   "title": "dev_lca.c DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_ioc) has no arm for four DOCUMENTED IOC registers -- STAT0 +0x040, STAT1 +0x060, SFT_RST +0x0c0, PAR_DIS +0x0e0 (HRM :10461, :10496) -- and S6.4.14 items 1-2 REQUIRE SROM to write SFT_RST and STAT0.  Before #518 those writes ended the process in default:; after #518 they survive as a once-announced declined write and a later read answers zero, not the written bits.  A strict improvement and still not the register: option-set member 7, IMPLEMENT (SFT_RST drives PCI rst_l; STAT0/STAT1 are the error log chapter 6 writes).  alpha_lcareg.h defines STAT0/STAT1 with field masks and has no SFT_RST.  Rung-3 witness constructible from lca_badval_probe.py's session shape.  *** REVISED 2026-09-10 by the codex design reading: STAT1 is RO with no W1C field; STAT0 is RO status plus W1C ERR/LOST only (mask 0x30); SFT_RST is a persistent WO reset control (RST=1 after reset, released by a written zero); PAR_DIS is WO.  Member 7 for STAT0+STAT1 (coupled), member 3 with a persistent bit for SFT_RST/PAR_DIS until PCI reset and parity exist; a uniform member-6 echo would be WRONG.  bus_pci has no reset entry point. ***",
   "note": "Filed 2026-09-10 by the grok seat on #518 pass 2; the #518 default-arm comment was corrected so it no longer calls these offsets unlisted.",
   "entries": [
    {
     "seat": "codex",
     "phase": "design",
     "d": "2026-09-10",
     "date": "2026-09-10",
     "grade": "REVISE-THE-FILING",
     "ev": "regress/artifacts/lcaiocstat0/codex_design_20260910.err",
     "grader": "main-loop (Fable 5.1)",
     "note": "GPT-6 Astra @ max, file-reading (handler, header, HRM sections, bus_pci, machine_alpha, emul.c); no refusal.  VERDICT: REVISE the proposed member-6 round -- a uniform store-and-echo would establish the WRONG contract.  Per register, with HRM lines: STAT0 +0x040 is RO status (P_NBR, CODE, TREF, THIT, CMD) plus R/W1C ERR[4] and LOST[5] (clearing mask 0x30), all bits UNDEFINED after reset, SROM writes ones to ERR/LOST (:10287-10370, :10271, :10788); STAT1 +0x060 is RO ADDR[31:0] with NO W1C field and S6.4.14 specifies no write to it (:10392-10409); SFT_RST +0x0c0 is WO RST[6] (mask 0x40), RST=1 after reset, a written one ASSERTS PCI reset until a written zero, SROM writes zero to release it (:10457-10489); PAR_DIS +0x0e0 is WO PAR[5] (mask 0x20) and does NOT suppress target-reported perr_l on CPU writes (:10509-10531).  WO must be added to the type vocabulary: echoing a WO value is emulator convention, never fidelity.  DISPOSITION: member 7 for STAT0 + STAT1 together (guest writes must never manufacture RO status; STAT1 captures the address while the error record is frozen), member 3 NOW for SFT_RST and PAR_DIS with a persistent bit until their effects exist -- so #518's default-arm decline is the right interim.  bus_pci has NO reset entry point or device reset callback (bus_pci.h:92-114, :146-162): SFT_RST costs an interface, not a call.  FOUND: the PCI backend already recognises an absent device and supplies no error to LCA (bus_pci.c:109-122; HRM :9494-9513 says hardware logs it in STAT0/STAT1) -- `nothing sets the logs' is missing integration, not absence.  The fork does not establish whether NetBSD or Linux touch these offsets; direct boot never executes the SROM sequence, so a functional reset model must arrange RELEASED PCI reset itself."
    }
   ]
  },
